 ## [Unreleased]
 
+- **Explain ambiguous accessor names.** Generation refuses grouped properties that would create duplicate PHP method names and identifies the properties to rename. Independent non-conflicting accessors remain available. Contributed by PHP Workbench downstream.
+
 - **Match generated method layout to its class.** Constructor and accessor actions preserve relative indentation and source line endings without rewriting captured defaults or documentation. Contributed by PHP Workbench downstream.
 
 - **Respect inherited generation contracts.** Generated accessors preserve inherited methods and compatible interface signatures. Constructor actions refuse to bypass inherited initialization or final constructor restrictions. Contributed by PHP Workbench downstream.
